  "details": "This is a longstanding bug, pretty much as far back as I can remember but it's finally my breaking point lol.\n\n1. Use a quest 2, air link or link cable.\n\n2. Load up vrchat through steam VR, oculus is my XR runtime but I think this bug is independent of that.\n\n3. While the game is initializing, place your headset off your head in a sideways / upside down orientation.\n\n4. Once the game has loaded, orient your headset correctly and put it on.\n\n5. Try and hit your controller  quick menu button. Open up the social panel or another floating panel from the quick menu. The floating menu will be locked at a slanted orientation. It wont be matching the global up vector for the scene. This will cause all other floating menu UI to be sideways or completely upside down until you full restart and try again.",
